{"name":"Club-Mate","hex":"#f8de7e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"club","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy object, often a kind of stick, intended for use as a bludgeoning weapon or a plaything.\n\n An implement to hit the ball in certain ball games, such as golf.\n An item used during routines, the apparatus consisting of a set of two clubs.","An implement to hit the ball in certain ball games, such as golf."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hit with a club.","To score a victory over by a large margin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/club"},{"term":"mate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fellow, comrade, colleague, partner or someone with whom something is shared, e.g. shipmate, classmate.","A breeding partner."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To match, fit together without space between.","To copulate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mate"}],"entries":[{"title":"Club-Mate","blocks":[{"text":"Club-Mate is a caffeinated carbonated mate-extract beverage made by the Loscher Brewery in Münchsteinach, Germany, which originated in 1924. Club-Mate has 20 mg of caffeine per 100 ml, sugar content of 5 g per 100 ml, and 20 kcal per 100 ml, which is lower than most energy drinks. Club-Mate is available in 0.33-litre and 0.5-litre bottles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/54/Club-Mate_Logo.svg/330px-Club-Mate_Logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Club-Mate"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Club-Mate.jpg/500px-Club-Mate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Club-Mate.jpg/1280px-Club-Mate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/C